{
  "id": "COMPOUND:21717 - PROTEIN:3897",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Ligustrone A may be involved in the regulation of Cholesteryl ester transfer protein (CETP) through multiple indirect pathways. The drug-target relationship is supported by the presence of Ligustrone A as a target of 8-O-(P-Coumaroyl)-1(10)E,4(5)E-Humuladien-8-Ol, which itself is a target of methyl (Z)-pentadec-8-enoate. These compounds are all linked to CETP, indicating a potential role in the metabolic regulation of lipid transport. Additionally, Ligustrone A is associated with HCT-8, a cell line that is also a target of 8-O-(P-Coumaroyl)-1(10)E,4(5)E-Humuladien-8-Ol, further reinforcing the connection between Ligustrone A and CETP. The scores from the paths suggest a consistent but not absolute relationship, with varying confidence levels across the evidence. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Ligustrone A to influence CETP through a network of targets, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
